# Security headers for static hosts that read this file (Netlify,
# Cloudflare Pages). If you deploy somewhere else (Vercel, Render static
# sites, S3+CloudFront, etc.), this file is silently ignored — use
# vercel.json (already included for Vercel) or your host's equivalent
# mechanism with these same header values. See README.md's Deploying
# section for per-host notes.
#
# CSP is intentionally not maximally strict on connect-src: Stream's
# Video/Chat SDK reaches a number of dynamically-selected regional edge
# servers for calling, not one fixed domain, so pinning connect-src to an
# exact allowlist risks silently breaking live calls the day Stream
# rebalances traffic. `https: wss:` still blocks the actual attack this
# header exists to stop (script-injected exfiltration to a non-https
# origin) without that fragility.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(self), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self' https: wss:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self' https://intranet.ridearrivo.com
